<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĭphātes</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νιφάτης</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A part of the Mount Taurus range in Armenia</i>,
			the mod. <i>Ali-Dagh</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3,
				30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2, 9, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 15,
				2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river that rises in the same</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			245</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 6, 409</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
